An over-long atomic string has no legal break point: the line stays
over-long, the string is neither split nor moved below its `:=` (the
issue-#85 no-gain guard), and a second format pass adds nothing
(fmt.max_line_length, feature.formatting A6). The DoProc line is the
catalog's own 93-column idempotent example, here indented.
-- input.ssl --
:PROCEDURE Notify;
:DECLARE sMessage;
sMessage := "This message text is long enough by itself to run past the ninety column limit easily";
DoProc("ThisIsAVeryLongProcedureNameArgumentThatByItselfPushesTheLineWellPastNinetyColumns");
:RETURN sMessage;
:ENDPROC;
-- format --
:PROCEDURE Notify;
	:DECLARE sMessage;
	sMessage := "This message text is long enough by itself to run past the ninety column limit easily";
	DoProc("ThisIsAVeryLongProcedureNameArgumentThatByItselfPushesTheLineWellPastNinetyColumns");
	:RETURN sMessage;
:ENDPROC;
-- diagnostics --
-- diagnostics [--strict --info] --
